// CASE 3 — THE ONE THAT DECIDES IT.
//
// Every language in the survey puts its unfinished-marker in BODY position.
// In B# a body needs a clause, and the only clause that does not force the
// author to invent a plausible pattern is a catch-all.
//
// But B# is not a single-body language — it is multi-clause with an
// exhaustiveness checker. So the question is whether writing that catch-all
// CONSUMES the residual that 23 §7 says is the whole value of a stub:
//
//   "a stub's residual is the entire declared parameter type, which is the
//    most informative diagnostic the language can produce"
//
// If this file compiles silently, then a body-position marker in B# buys
// legality by destroying exactly the information the marker exists to expose.
module StubCatchall

type FrameType = :method | :header | :body | :heartbeat

public int Weigh(FrameType f)

Weigh(_) -> 0
